  "reply": "Done.\n\n- **slug.py**: rewrote `slugify` to match SPEC.md — lowercases, collapses every run of non-alphanumeric characters into one `-`, trims leading/trailing separators, and returns `\"item\"` when nothing alphanumeric remains (covers the old gaps: no collapsing of `!!!`/`___` runs, no trimming of non-space separators, no fallback).\n- **tests/test_slug.py**: added regression tests for the documented edge cases (separator-run collapsing/trimming like `\"---A___B---\" → \"a-b\"` and `\"  Hello,   World!! \"`, the `\"item\"` fallback, lowercasing, and empty string) — 7 `def test_` methods, exceeding the ≥3 requirement.\n- `SPEC.md` and `acceptance.py` untouched.\n\nThe acceptance assertions all hold against the new implementation, and the unittest suite passes.",
